{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he did not go as time after time.</b> He did not go <b>toward necromancies</b> and trials from place to place this time, as he had done another time, for he knew it would avail him nothing — for he saw no serpent in Jacob — and he intended to bless them, and HaShem concurred through him, as it is written: ותהי עליו רוח אלקים." "<b>And he set his face toward the wilderness.</b> That is the steppes of Moab, where Israel were."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:29.643173821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}